==Player Feedback and Our Changes (June 22nd)==
{|class=wikitable style="text-align:center; width:665px;"
!Your Feedback
!Our Actions
|-
|The Ash Sanctifier provides too much value considering its cost when compared to similar items. Currently 1 Death Rune grants the sanctifier 100 charges.
|Following player feedback and further balancing, we agree that this is a little too generous. We'd like to change this to 10 Death Runes per 100 charges instead.
|-
|Some Demons in the game have very high Magic levels, (e.g Skotizo and K'ril Tsutsaroth) so Magic spells feel very weak against them. This makes Demonbane Spells feel less rewarding to use against popular Demons, even though it should be a viable option.
|The intention of the Arceuus Spellbook rework was to increase variety in viable options, rather than entirely replace existing metas.

We feel the spellbook has achieved this, though we do agree that Demonbane spells could be improved slightly. As such, we'll be looking to increase the accuracy of these spells.

Currently, accuracy is 25% with Mark of Darkness. We will be changing this so that the base accuracy without Mark of Darkness will be increased from 0% to 20%. With Mark of Darkness, accuracy will be increased from 25% to 40%.

We're hopeful this change will make using Demonbane spells feel more worthwhile.
|-
|All Demons in the game now consistently drop Ashes. As a result of this, tasks in the Catacombs of Kourend such as Hellhounds and Mutated Bloodvelds no longer provide passive Prayer restoration, as they do not drop bones that can be buried or crushed with the Bonecrusher.
|Demons droping Ashes instead of bones is intentional and now consistent with their lore. We'd like to keep it this way to maintain consistency across the game.

However, we understand this has impacted an established playstyle that players may not have considered when we proposed the changes.

The best solution we've seen so far is to allow Bloodvelds and Hellhounds to drop bones alongside the Ashes they would also drop. Whilst not ideal from a lore perspective, we'd be willing to compromise on this based on your feedback.

Let us know what you think. Should these demons also drop bones in conjunction with their ashes?
|-
|The Harmonised Staff is less viable in certain PvM situations such as The Nightmare of Ashihama and Zulrah. This is because generally it is now more worthwhile for players to use other Magic weapons that are compatible with the Arceuus Spellbook which grants access to Thralls.
|We'd like to thank you for all your suggestions so far about what we should do. We still haven't come to a decision on what would be best and we welcome you to suggest further improvements for changes to the Harmonised Staff that we could include in a future poll.
|-
|Some players feel the Demonic Offering spell is not viable to use during combat due to the spell being interruptable.
|We'll be removing the ability for monsters to interrupt Demonic Offering. This should make it feel better to use while you're in combat.

We could also look at shortening the animations used with these spells, whilst adding a cool-down between casts to preserve the experience rates that were polled when outside of combat.

Let us know what you think of these changes!
|-
|Dark Lure can feel frustrating to use against Implings. Sometimes an Impling will float towards the player as expected and sometimes they will drift off in an inconsistent manner.
|In tomorrow's game update we'll be making some changes that will improve the behaviour of Implings under the effects of Dark Lure. When hit with Dark Lure, Implings will immediately try to follow the player for a total of 6 seconds (including the time it takes to reach the player). Afterwards, they'll roam around the player in a 5x5 grid. Hopefully these changes make using the spell feel much better!
|-
|Some players have expressed issues with the mechanics of Thralls in certain locations across the game.
|We would like to clarify that Thralls are intended to stay present in the area you have summoned them and have purposefully been designed to not move around too much.

Whilst the mechanics of Thralls will not be changing drastically, we have noticed a few of the issues with their behaviour that we'll be resolving as part of our standard bug-fixing procedure.

Keep an eye out on future Game Update newspost for more information about these fixes and please continue reporting any bugs in-game and we will continue to investigate them on a case-by-case basis.
|-
|Players would like to hang the Kourend Map in the Quest Hall.
|Sure, why not! We've added this into our backlog for a future release.

In the meantime, we'll also investigate the feasibility of updating the maps graphically!
|-
|Players have suggested various ways we can improve the A Kingdom Divided quest through small tweaks and changes to dialogue, etc.
|We appreciate your feedback on how we can improve the quest even more! Your suggestions have been passed to the relevant team and you should expect to see some minor tweaks and changes in the coming weeks!
|}

